WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
The safety value is the worst safety signal along a future trajectory.

00:08.000 --> 00:16.000
A push disturbs the humanoid. The video marks the early warning, followed by loss of balance.

00:16.000 --> 00:30.000
Safe and unsafe balance trials are shown side by side in slow motion, above their safety-value traces.

00:30.000 --> 00:49.000
Two camera views show safe and unsafe ball-avoidance trials. The predicted safety value becomes positive before the collision.

00:49.000 --> 01:41.000
Diagrams compare safety Bellman updates and full-trajectory targets, illustrating slow propagation in one-step learning.

01:41.000 --> 02:28.000
The lambda-Reachability estimator samples a geometric horizon and bootstraps at the terminal state with a horizon-dependent probability.

02:28.000 --> 02:47.000
Simulation clips compare multi-step lambda learning and one-step learning for balance and collision tasks.

02:47.000 --> 02:59.349
Hardware collision footage and plots compare the lambda safety value, the one-step baseline, and the measured safety signal.
